      "username": "doppelgangerung",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/doppelgangerung/{size}/1876_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-12-15T06:05:39.760Z",
      "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/f/f9e902cca037998ccbb7247f7bc775a23c005772.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/f9e902cca037998ccbb7247f7bc775a23c005772\" title=\"Screenshot_20221212-234728\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/f9e902cca037998ccbb7247f7bc775a23c005772_2_219x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Screenshot_20221212-234728\" data-base62-sha1=\"zEO73jW8YgusDWMOtEPXU8A4L4u\" width=\"219\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/f9e902cca037998ccbb7247f7bc775a23c005772_2_219x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/f9e902cca037998ccbb7247f7bc775a23c005772_2_328x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/f9e902cca037998ccbb7247f7bc775a23c005772_2_438x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/f/f9e902cca037998ccbb7247f7bc775a23c005772_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot_20221212-234728</span><span class=\"informations\">1080×2460 164 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div><br>\nThe Wrath Of Khan intro was a nice touch, in light of Kirstie Alley’s recent passing - as for the fight itself, it wasn’t as quick as some were able to pull off, but by turns three and four Setback and Lifeline were generating enough global damage between them to render the Manifestations vulnerable to Infinitor’s Whispers of Oblivion, clearing the board and ending the game.</p>",
